AB  - The emergence of the computing power networks (CPNs) has brought massive heterogeneous data together while promoting the efficiency of computing power via the cloud-edgeterminal structure. These data are scattered in the independent data centers deploying different database/lakehouse environment within the CPN, reminding people of a federated approach to achieve data sharing and federated governance. However, none implementation of federated data management system among data lakehouses has been witnessed so far for CPNs, which restricts the effective utilization of these data. To this end, FedLakehouse is proposed, which achieves federated data management among heterogeneous lakehouses and relational databases. Providing a unified data access view, FedLakehouse can realize many common commands among heterogeneous lakehouses and databases. The proposed framework shows the ability of federated data management among heterogeneous (distributed) database systems and puts forward a strong support for many training applications in the computing power networks. © 2025 IEEE.
