AB  - For better business analytical processing, data warehouses are a helpful system. Most of the government departments, academic institutions and other businesses such as warehouse are necessary to promote their business. This study proposes some data modelling practices for handling a possible future epidemic. It shows the technical steps to develop the system like the processes of extraction, transformation and loading of data and generating an error event table. Several data are collected from concerned sources. It uses the cube format for modelling the data and viewing the data up to the granular level. It uses energy-efficient FP-growth algorithm to predict a new pattern for a possible ‘unknown epidemic. The energy-efficient FP algorithm uses a compressed representation of the database. It uses a ‘bag of jobs’ algorithm for quick execution of groups of operations. The study uses probabilistic clustering for forming the data marts on the demand of the users. It generates several reports to support the authority to handle such an epidemic in a better way. It may enable the users or policymakers to generate several reports to examine the real-time situation and manage policies towards a better future. © 2021, The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd.
