AB  - The synergization of the Internet of things (IoT) and Machine Learning (ML) has vast potential, but sustainable smart systems, but most of the time, it is constrained through a disjointed methodology that sees the collection of data and the intelligence of the model as independent two factors. The paper presents the Data-Centric Intelligence (DCI) framework, which is the comprehensive paradigm to remove this divide by maximizing the entire sizable data to actionable sustainability results pipeline. The DCI framework achieves a multimodal IoT data fabric to create robust ingestion, apply automated data-centric principles such as validation and lightweight feature engineering at the edge to guarantee data quality, and predictive analytics with adaptive ML models such as LSTM networks. It provides a closed-loop decision support system, which translates the insights of the models into real-time control of the resources, and it is the essence of its core equipment to develop a feedback system of constant system improvement. We test the framework with precision agriculture pilot, in which it captured a 25 percent saving on water consumption and a 15 percent saving on fertilizer application, and a smart building many, which resulted in an improvement of 20 percent in energy efficiency. This work proposes an easily scalable model of increasing the productivity and environmental sustainability of future smart systems by smoothly integrating data, intelligence, and action. ©2026 IEEE.
