AB  - Cloud-integrated lighting management uses Internet of Things (IoT) technologies to improve warehouse energy efficiency. The research examines how warehouse lighting systems might improve energy use using IoT devices and sensors. To create a smart lighting management system that adjusts to warehouse demands using real-time data and cloud-based analytics. The IoT-driven technology monitors occupancy, ambient light, and other characteristics via sensors. The sensors provide data to a cloud platform for real-time processing. The cloud-based solution optimizes energy use by dynamically adjusting lighting settings using occupancy-based management and daylight harvesting. An intelligent and adaptable lighting system that illuminates warehouse activity and minimizes energy consumption and expenses is the aim. The research found that warehouses with IoT-based lighting control may save a lot of electricity. Cloud-based solutions provide scalability, flexibility, and remote management, making them promising for large-scale industrial settings. The system may improve energy efficiency in commercial and industrial settings, contributing to sustainable practices. Smart and connected solutions are essential for current warehouse energy issues.  © 2024 IEEE.
