AB  - The growing adoption of digital technologies is reshaping how buildings are managed. Still, low data quality remains a key challenge. Incomplete or inaccurate data can compromise decisions and hinder compliance with regulations. The work presented here, tested on ten pilot buildings across Europe, significantly improves data quality, raising completeness from 55% to 100%, while improving accuracy. A centralized data lake ensures seamless integration of static and dynamic sources, enabling real-time insights. Beyond technical gains, the solution supports the goals of the Energy Performance of Buildings Directive, enhancing energy efficiency and sustainability through better data governance and scalable, replicable management models. © 2025, European Council on Computing in Construction (EC3). All rights reserved.
